    },
    {
      "id": 96,
      "start": 220.16,
      "end": 220.94,
      "en": "It's a hole that is usually long.",
      "zh": "这是一个通常很长的洞。"
    },
    {
      "id": 97,
      "start": 221.28,
      "end": 224.08,
      "en": "Long and it's like a rectangular hole.",
      "zh": "长，它就像一个矩形孔。"
    },
    {
      "id": 98,
      "start": 224.32,
      "end": 225.32,
      "en": "Yeah.",
      "zh": "对。"
    },
    {
      "id": 99,
      "start": 225.32,
      "end": 226.14,
      "en": "A slot is never a circle.",
      "zh": "插槽永远不是一个圆圈。"
    },
    {
      "id": 100,
      "start": 226.56,
      "end": 226.74,
      "en": "Okay.",
      "zh": "好的。"
    },
    {
      "id": 101,
      "start": 227.56,
      "end": 232.12,
      "en": "So for example, when you get mail, the mailman will put it into your mailbox through the slot.",
      "zh": "例如，当您收到邮件时，邮递员会通过插槽将其放入您的邮箱。"
    },
    {
      "id": 102,
      "start": 232.56,
      "end": 232.84,
      "en": "That's right.",
      "zh": "没错。"
    },
    {
      "id": 103,
      "start": 233.18,
      "end": 233.4,
      "en": "Okay.",
      "zh": "好的。"
    },
    {
      "id": 104,
      "start": 233.84,
      "end": 240.76,
      "en": "And now that he put his card into the slot, he had to input a six digit pin code.",
      "zh": "而现在他将卡放入插槽中，他必须输入一个六位数的 PIN 码。"
    },
    {
      "id": 105,
      "start": 241.09,
      "end": 242.27,
      "en": "Want to just do both together?",
      "zh": "想一起做吗？"
    },
    {
      "id": 106,
      "start": 242.84,
      "end": 243.17,
      "en": "Digit and pin code?",
      "zh": "数字和 PIN 码？"
    },
    {
      "id": 107,
      "start": 243.84,
      "end": 244.84,
      "en": "Yeah.",
      "zh": "对。"
    },
    {
      "id": 108,
      "start": 244.84,
      "end": 245.84,
      "en": "Okay.",
      "zh": "好的。"
    },
    {
      "id": 109,
      "start": 245.84,
      "end": 246.84,
      "en": "So a six digit pin code.",
      "zh": "所以一个六位数的PIN码。"
    },
    {
      "id": 110,
      "start": 246.84,
      "end": 247.84,
      "en": "All right.",
      "zh": "好的。"
    },
    {
      "id": 111,
      "start": 247.84,
      "end": 248.69,
      "en": "Now we have two words here that are new.",
      "zh": "现在我们有两个新词。"
    },
    {
      "id": 112,
      "start": 249.4,
      "end": 250.4,
      "en": "Digit.",
      "zh": "数字。"
    },
    {
      "id": 113,
      "start": 250.4,
      "end": 253.41,
      "en": "Digit is basically a number between zero and nine.",
      "zh": "数字基本上是一个介于零和九之间的数字。"
    },
    {
      "id": 114,
      "start": 253.76,
      "end": 253.97,
      "en": "Okay.",
      "zh": "好的。"
    },
    {
      "id": 115,
      "start": 254.03,
      "end": 257.47,
      "en": "So any number between zero and nine is considered a digit.",
      "zh": "因此，零到九之间的任何数字都被认为是一个数字。"
    },
    {
      "id": 116,
